WEBVTT

00:04.504 --> 00:06.923
[intriguing music playing]

00:08.008 --> 00:10.301
SWEET HOME

00:10.385 --> 00:12.345
[En] These are the nigiri sushi I made.

00:12.429 --> 00:15.932
I can't believe you're treating me
to your home cooking, Mr. En!

00:16.016 --> 00:17.726
Yeah... Now eat up.

00:17.809 --> 00:19.352
I love Nigiri with raw meat.

00:19.436 --> 00:21.813
And you cut the meat
in the shape of a mushroom.

00:21.896 --> 00:23.606
That's so you, En.

00:23.690 --> 00:25.608
[Ebisu] Can I just eat
the meat off the top?

00:26.234 --> 00:27.110
Nom!

00:27.193 --> 00:28.111
Mm!

00:28.194 --> 00:29.612
[gnawing loudly]

00:29.696 --> 00:31.531
[Fujita] Mmm, mm!

00:31.614 --> 00:33.366
Oh my! It's delicious, sir!

00:33.450 --> 00:36.119
- [Nikaido] It's so fatty!
- [Ebisu] Can I get some extra sauce?

00:37.954 --> 00:40.248
- [Ebisu] Whoa! [gasps]
- What?! Where are we?!

00:40.331 --> 00:43.001
- The sushi's gone! [screaming]
- There's nothing here!

00:43.084 --> 00:46.046
Hang on. Somebody must have used magic

00:46.129 --> 00:48.506
to erase everything
except the three of us!

00:49.466 --> 00:52.260
- Mr. Chota, long time no see.
- Huh?

00:52.969 --> 00:56.056
[gasps] I'm back to normal!

00:56.139 --> 00:59.684
[En] Everybody relax.
This is just a dream.

00:59.768 --> 01:00.935
[Fujita] Mr. En!

01:01.019 --> 01:02.437
So we're in a dream!?

01:02.520 --> 01:04.105
That sushi topping from earlier

01:04.189 --> 01:07.567
was actually a new kind of mushroom
harvested on my farm.

01:08.151 --> 01:10.570
I call it "Dream Machine."

01:10.653 --> 01:13.073
- Aa-hah!
- So, it wasn't raw meat? That's gross!

01:13.156 --> 01:17.577
The inside looks just like meat,
doesn't it? The taste is similar as well.

01:18.787 --> 01:20.205
When you eat this mushroom,

01:20.288 --> 01:24.417
you fall into a deep sleep
and can create any dream you want.

01:24.501 --> 01:27.212
And if multiple people eat it
at the same time,

01:27.295 --> 01:28.671
they enter the same dream.

01:28.755 --> 01:29.589
[Ebisu] Ah?!

01:29.672 --> 01:33.718
Next month, I plan to launch it
under my food brand.

01:33.802 --> 01:36.805
I had you all serve as test subjects.

01:36.888 --> 01:38.723
Whatever dream I want...

01:39.224 --> 01:40.517
So that would mean...

01:40.600 --> 01:42.268
[macho groaning]

01:43.394 --> 01:46.523
[deep voice] This is awesome!
Long live the Dream Machine!

01:47.107 --> 01:48.817
Anyone else think he's too big?

01:49.901 --> 01:51.861
Nikaido, why do you look like Chota?

01:51.945 --> 01:52.779
Huh?

01:52.862 --> 01:55.782
[hesitating] Maybe it's because
I was thinking about Chota!

01:55.865 --> 01:57.075
Yeah, that's it!

01:57.575 --> 02:01.579
He hasn't been around here lately,
so I thought you were missing him.

02:01.663 --> 02:02.664
[giggles]

02:02.747 --> 02:05.375
[En] That's impossible. Go back to normal.

02:05.458 --> 02:07.377
- You're an eyesore.
- [Nikaido] Huh? Oh.

02:08.086 --> 02:10.964
- [crunching underfoot]
- Huh? Is this Hole?

02:11.047 --> 02:14.217
- Bouncy, bouncy, bouncy.
- [En] It's even filthy in my dream.

02:14.300 --> 02:16.344
[intriguing music playing]

02:16.928 --> 02:17.846
[En] Ugh.

02:17.929 --> 02:21.099
It's that lizard guy...
But why are there two Nikaidos?

02:22.976 --> 02:24.352
[Fujita growls ferociously]

02:25.311 --> 02:26.813
Mr. En! Step back!

02:29.399 --> 02:31.067
- [lively music playing]
- [straining]

02:36.656 --> 02:38.241
[laughing maniacally]

02:38.324 --> 02:41.828
How's that, boss?
Long live the Dream Machine!

02:41.911 --> 02:43.329
- [laughing maniacally]
- Ugh.

02:43.830 --> 02:45.957
Ebisu, your dream is...

02:46.833 --> 02:48.334
Right, never mind.

02:48.960 --> 02:53.631
I knew this would be a hit with people
dissatisfied with reality, like Fujita.

02:54.132 --> 02:56.467
Nikaido, what do you wish for?

02:57.135 --> 02:58.970
Huh? What's wrong?

02:59.053 --> 03:00.597
I hate you, En!

03:00.680 --> 03:02.182
What are you so angry about?!

03:02.265 --> 03:04.934
- Hey, Nikaido!
- [Ebisu] My shoulders are getting sore.

03:05.018 --> 03:08.271
- [Fujita laughing]
- Fujita, you're my number one guy!

03:08.354 --> 03:10.607
I leave all my fortune to you!

03:10.690 --> 03:12.734
I've admired you this whole time.

03:13.651 --> 03:15.028
[Ebisu sighs]

03:18.615 --> 03:20.617
Oh! Oh...

03:20.700 --> 03:22.660
[intriguing music playing]

03:24.454 --> 03:26.372
Is... that me?

03:26.456 --> 03:28.291
[airplane whooshing overhead]

03:29.167 --> 03:30.001
Oh!

03:31.211 --> 03:32.253
Wait!

03:37.050 --> 03:38.760
This house...

03:42.972 --> 03:44.015
Oh...

03:45.600 --> 03:47.018
This mask...

03:47.852 --> 03:49.979
It's my mask from back then.

03:50.688 --> 03:51.564
Oh...

04:00.990 --> 04:03.076
- [knocking on door]
- [woman] Ebisu.

04:03.159 --> 04:04.327
- [door opens]
- [Ebisu gasps]

04:04.410 --> 04:06.788
Are your magic studies going well?

04:06.871 --> 04:09.374
[man] I'm counting on you, Ebisu.

04:12.543 --> 04:14.671
[Ebisu] Mom... Dad...

04:17.215 --> 04:19.259
[laughing maniacally]

04:19.342 --> 04:21.386
Long live the Dream Machine!

04:21.469 --> 04:24.597
I'd be unstoppable
if I ate this every night!

04:24.681 --> 04:25.640
Aaah!

04:25.723 --> 04:28.559
That floor better be sparkling, Ebisu!

04:28.643 --> 04:30.395
[Ebisu] Yes, Master.

04:30.478 --> 04:33.523
Boss, the dinner preparations
are complete.

04:33.606 --> 04:35.149
I could get used to this!

04:35.233 --> 04:38.403
[both laughing maniacally]

04:38.486 --> 04:39.779
[gasps]

04:40.947 --> 04:42.865
Wait... this is...?!

04:42.949 --> 04:44.993
- [En] Have you taken out the trash yet?
- [gasps]

04:45.076 --> 04:47.662
[Ebisu] We should dispose of
that useless raw garbage.

04:47.745 --> 04:48.997
Yes, Mr. En.

04:49.080 --> 04:51.082
Uh... Mr. En?

04:51.582 --> 04:53.751
Mr. En?! You guys!

04:53.835 --> 04:57.297
Hang on! It's me, Fujita! Wait...

04:58.339 --> 05:00.758
Wait for me! Nikaido!

05:05.096 --> 05:06.723
[gasps] A hair dryer?!

05:06.806 --> 05:07.765
[gasps]

05:07.849 --> 05:09.058
[hair dryer blowing]

05:09.142 --> 05:10.518
[En] Stop it!

05:10.601 --> 05:13.479
Mushrooms are weak to hot air, you know!

05:15.606 --> 05:17.400
[En grunts] This is...

05:18.026 --> 05:21.154
This is the scene deep down
I fear more than anything!

05:21.237 --> 05:23.573
A true nightmare!

05:23.656 --> 05:27.160
So the Dream Machine
has effects like this too!

05:27.243 --> 05:29.162
[strained groaning]

05:29.245 --> 05:30.663
[jeering laughter]

05:30.747 --> 05:32.749
[En gasps] No...

05:32.832 --> 05:34.042
I'm shriveling!

05:35.251 --> 05:36.169
[gasps]

05:36.919 --> 05:38.463
[groaning]

05:39.255 --> 05:40.965
The Dream Machine is a mushroom

05:41.049 --> 05:45.553
that allows you to understand yourself
in various unexpected ways...

05:46.054 --> 05:50.558
Now then, lucky test subjects,
what do ya think? Will this sell?

05:50.641 --> 05:52.935
[tearfully] I mean, who can say?

05:53.019 --> 05:56.522
- [Fujita sobbing]
- [Ebisu] Mom... Dad...

07:24.986 --> 07:26.904
THE BEGINNING

07:28.156 --> 07:29.449
[Risu groaning]

07:29.532 --> 07:30.992
Ow...

07:31.075 --> 07:32.368
Figures...

07:33.494 --> 07:35.121
Dokuga, huh.

07:35.204 --> 07:37.999
That bastard could've killed me,
but he didn't.

07:38.499 --> 07:40.626
I understand everything now,

07:40.710 --> 07:43.504
The guy who killed me,
and the reason he did it...

07:44.005 --> 07:45.840
Damn Cross-Eyes...

07:46.340 --> 07:49.635
Why'd I even join a group like this
in the first place?

07:51.095 --> 07:52.430
Ever since I was a kid,

07:52.513 --> 07:55.558
I've never been able to produce
any magical smoke at all.

07:56.142 --> 07:59.687
Of course, it turned out
there were lots like me out there.

07:59.770 --> 08:02.732
Or guys who can produce smoke,
but only a tiny bit,

08:02.815 --> 08:04.859
or guys with useless magic...

08:05.401 --> 08:07.820
Yeah, a bunch of guys like that...

08:07.904 --> 08:10.072
That's who the Cross-Eyes were.

08:10.740 --> 08:12.575
[Cross-Eyes 1] Elite bastard!

08:12.658 --> 08:17.079
Stuffing his face with fancy food
in this high-end restaurant! Ugh!

08:17.163 --> 08:20.583
- Hey, Risu, help me out.
- Yeah.

08:20.666 --> 08:22.502
[both straining]

08:25.463 --> 08:27.089
[Cross-Eyes 1] All right. Off you go.

08:31.677 --> 08:35.640
Hey Risu, listen,
any idea where they take 'em?

08:36.098 --> 08:39.810
[Risu] I know where. The bodies go to
the research facility in Berith Village.

08:39.894 --> 08:42.188
And the heads go to the boss,
is that right?

08:42.271 --> 08:45.149
The boss uses
those elite sorcerers' bodies

08:45.233 --> 08:49.195
to turn himself into
the strongest sorcerer around.

08:49.278 --> 08:52.907
All that, as a way to save us,
his own people.

08:52.990 --> 08:55.326
Check this out. This is black powder.

08:55.409 --> 08:57.954
I got it as a reward for the job!

08:58.037 --> 08:59.497
Watch this.

09:01.374 --> 09:04.335
[inhales deeply, sighs, groaning]

09:08.881 --> 09:11.133
[Risu] The black powder was our hope.

09:11.842 --> 09:16.222
But, of course,
even that black powder didn't work on me.

09:16.889 --> 09:20.935
[Cross-Eyes 1] Hey, Risu,
what are you spending your pay on?

09:21.018 --> 09:24.230
[Risu] Actually,
I'm thinking about going to school.

09:24.313 --> 09:26.857
[Cross-Eyes 1] School?
Are you serious? [laughing]

09:26.941 --> 09:28.317
SOUTH ZAGAN MAGIC TRAINING SCHOOL

09:28.401 --> 09:30.319
[Risu] I was serious.

09:30.403 --> 09:34.156
If I studied at school,
maybe even I could produce some smoke...

09:34.240 --> 09:36.325
[teacher] Let me introduce a new student.

09:36.409 --> 09:40.705
- This is Risu, who joined the class today.
- Nice to meet you.

09:40.788 --> 09:42.123
You see his eyes?

09:42.206 --> 09:45.084
- Yeah. He's got the cross-eyes.
- What's he trying to pull?

09:45.167 --> 09:48.004
[teacher] Now then, I'll begin the lesson.

09:48.087 --> 09:51.090
[strained groaning]

09:52.174 --> 09:53.509
I did it! I did it!

09:53.593 --> 09:56.012
- [teacher] You bastard! That was pathetic!
- Ah!

09:56.637 --> 09:57.930
[teacher] You're lacking spirit!

09:58.014 --> 10:01.058
Sure, like this is really gonna
help me use magic...

10:01.142 --> 10:03.269
I've thrown my pay down the drain.

10:03.352 --> 10:05.771
- [panting]
- [teacher] Who told you to sit down?!

10:05.855 --> 10:08.274
- [gasps]
- [teacher] Damn pathetic fool!

10:08.357 --> 10:10.735
Asshole! Who does he think he is?

10:10.818 --> 10:13.237
[teacher] Spirit! Spir-- [groans]

10:13.321 --> 10:15.239
A... Aikawa!

10:15.823 --> 10:18.743
Hey, Teach... you getting cranky?

10:18.826 --> 10:21.287
Should I share a bit of my lunch with you?

10:21.370 --> 10:22.747
[teacher moaning softly]

10:22.830 --> 10:25.833
[teacher] It's self-study today!
Self-study, I said!

10:25.916 --> 10:27.752
[students cheering, laughing]

10:27.835 --> 10:30.588
[student] Aikawa... Thank you so much.

10:30.671 --> 10:32.590
Hey, don't mention it.

10:32.673 --> 10:35.426
Just buy me something for lunch,
and we're good!

10:35.509 --> 10:36.594
[student chuckles uneasily]

10:36.677 --> 10:40.765
[student 2] Buy him lunch,
classic Aikawa! [giggling]

10:40.848 --> 10:42.099
Huh.

10:43.809 --> 10:47.229
Hmph... So then, Risu.
You having fun at school?

10:47.313 --> 10:50.566
Yeah, I guess.
The other guys seem pretty chill.

10:51.901 --> 10:55.196
[Cross-Eyes 1] Remember, you don't get
to use magic just by studying.

10:55.279 --> 10:56.447
[zipper closes]

10:56.947 --> 10:58.449
Did you hear, Risu?

10:58.532 --> 11:01.952
Apparently, the group just bought
this apartment building.

11:02.036 --> 11:04.080
I wonder who's gonna live here.

11:04.163 --> 11:07.458
[Cross-Eyes 1] Who knows?
Probably some of the higher-ups?

11:08.459 --> 11:09.335
[teacher] Well,

11:09.418 --> 11:11.837
as you can see, rare magic

11:11.921 --> 11:16.425
includes those that manipulate
restoration, life, time, and so on.

11:16.509 --> 11:17.593
- Therefore...
- [Aikawa] Hey.

11:18.302 --> 11:22.306
Haven't seen Maruyama and Tachibana?
They haven't been coming to school.

11:22.390 --> 11:24.517
Now that you mention it... yeah.

11:24.600 --> 11:27.103
Shimamura from class three vanished too.

11:27.186 --> 11:29.397
[student 3] Hi sir. Sorry, we're late.

11:30.731 --> 11:34.110
[Aikawa] Hey! What happened to you guys?
Your faces!

11:34.193 --> 11:35.319
[chuckles nervously]

11:35.403 --> 11:37.196
We just fell down that's all.

11:37.279 --> 11:38.572
[Aikawa sighs]

11:39.573 --> 11:41.992
- [teacher] Also, in extremely rare cases...
- [Aikawa growls]

11:42.076 --> 11:44.745
...there are sorcerers who possess
the power of a "curse."

11:44.829 --> 11:47.289
If anyone really had a power like that,

11:47.373 --> 11:49.500
the Cross-Eyes would never
leave 'em alone.

11:49.583 --> 11:52.253
[student 4] Oh, there you are. Risu!

11:52.336 --> 11:53.963
The teacher's calling for you.

11:54.046 --> 11:55.756
Huh? Me?

11:55.840 --> 11:57.341
[knocking on door]

11:57.425 --> 11:59.260
Excuse me... [gasps]

11:59.343 --> 12:01.762
- Ah, new guy, you came.
- [student 5 whimpering]

12:01.846 --> 12:03.931
[teacher] Well then, come in.

12:05.349 --> 12:06.225
STUDENT ROSTER

12:06.308 --> 12:10.020
According to the documents,
you can't produce smoke at all.

12:10.104 --> 12:11.272
That right, Risu?

12:12.356 --> 12:13.941
- Yeah.
- [teacher] I see.

12:14.024 --> 12:16.068
Even with perfect attendance,

12:16.152 --> 12:19.613
there's no telling how long
it'll take you take to graduate.

12:20.281 --> 12:21.449
It may get rough.

12:22.366 --> 12:23.951
And now, here's the thing.

12:24.034 --> 12:26.162
As your educational material,

12:26.245 --> 12:29.206
you'll be buying
this "Magic Power Bracelet."

12:29.290 --> 12:32.042
Pay 50,000 nicks.

12:32.126 --> 12:33.377
If you wear this,

12:33.461 --> 12:36.464
you'll be able to produce smoke
in no time.

12:37.047 --> 12:41.218
Unbelievable, our own damn teacher
selling fake trinkets.

12:41.302 --> 12:43.554
You little shit!
How dare you defy-- [groans]

12:44.388 --> 12:46.557
[pained screaming, groaning]

12:47.183 --> 12:49.560
Your empty threats won't work
on me, you know.

12:49.643 --> 12:53.397
[teacher] You bastard.
I won't forgive you! Get out of here!

12:54.482 --> 12:57.651
[Aikawa] I heard that.
I totally heard that.

12:57.735 --> 12:59.653
[teacher] Aikawa! You bastard!

12:59.737 --> 13:01.572
[Aikawa] Knew it was you. [chuckles]

13:01.655 --> 13:04.408
You're the reason everyone's
been getting hurt and disappearing.

13:06.619 --> 13:09.622
[teacher] Aikawa!
You've always been a nuisance...

13:10.706 --> 13:12.374
Vanish into nothing!

13:17.671 --> 13:19.423
[quizzical music playing]

13:19.507 --> 13:24.929
[Aikawa sighs] What do we do with him?
If he wakes up, we might get expelled.

13:25.012 --> 13:26.722
- [Risu] We're fine.
- Huh?

13:26.806 --> 13:28.516
I've got an idea.

13:30.810 --> 13:33.729
- I'm counting on you.
- Yeah, see you around.

13:33.813 --> 13:34.939
[horn beeps]

13:35.022 --> 13:37.149
[Aikawa] Uh, where's that truck going?

13:37.233 --> 13:39.735
Some things, you don't need to know.

13:40.319 --> 13:42.530
[Aikawa] Still, you really saved me.

13:42.613 --> 13:45.157
That bastard was related to the principal.

13:45.241 --> 13:49.745
If you hadn't stood up to him, oof,
I wouldn't have been able to do anything.

13:50.329 --> 13:51.455
Thanks.

13:52.832 --> 13:54.750
I just have a short fuse, that's all.

13:55.835 --> 13:57.753
I'm Aikawa. Nice to meet you.

13:59.630 --> 14:02.007
Nice to meet you too. I'm Risu.

14:04.009 --> 14:07.429
[Risu] Aikawa...
Where the hell have you gone?

14:07.513 --> 14:08.514
[door opening]

14:08.597 --> 14:10.307
So you're awake, Risu.

14:10.391 --> 14:13.269
[Risu] Yo, Dokuga,
I've been wanting to see you.

14:13.352 --> 14:15.771
There's something I wanna ask you.

14:15.855 --> 14:20.150
Wouldn't it have been better
if we just killed this bastard, Dokuga?

14:20.234 --> 14:22.778
He probably came here
to steal something anyway.

14:22.862 --> 14:25.197
There's nothing here worth anything.

14:25.281 --> 14:29.910
Don't get it twisted now, Saji.
It's not that he "chose" not to kill me.

14:30.536 --> 14:32.162
It's that he couldn't.

14:32.246 --> 14:37.042
- [gasps]
- [Risu] Ain't that right, Dokuga?

14:38.127 --> 14:39.461
BOARDING AND DISEMBARKING

14:39.545 --> 14:40.546
Huh, ah!

14:41.338 --> 14:42.298
[giggles]

14:42.381 --> 14:45.050
We finally made it to Zagan City.

14:45.134 --> 14:47.553
And it's night-time already!

14:47.636 --> 14:48.554
- Um...
- Huh?

14:49.680 --> 14:50.764
[Nikaido] Caiman?

14:51.557 --> 14:53.058
- [Caiman grunts]
- [Nikaido] No, Caiman!

14:53.142 --> 14:54.059
[Caiman panting]

14:57.897 --> 15:00.316
This road... I remember this!

15:01.233 --> 15:03.068
[breathing heavily, gasps]

15:03.152 --> 15:06.572
[panting]

15:08.908 --> 15:11.577
MEMORIES KEEP CIRCLING ROUND AND ROUND

15:13.787 --> 15:16.290
This is Zagan Magic Training School.

15:17.875 --> 15:20.419
Ah! Ah, my head!

15:21.003 --> 15:22.922
- [Nikaido] Caiman!
- [Natsuki] Big Bro!

15:23.005 --> 15:26.425
- Caiman! What's wrong? You just... Huh?
- [Caiman groaning]

15:27.384 --> 15:29.720
[Nikaido] Is this a school?

15:30.262 --> 15:32.056
It's abandoned.

15:32.139 --> 15:34.516
Big Bro, why did you come here?

15:34.600 --> 15:37.686
[groans] I've got
unfinished business inside.

15:38.812 --> 15:42.191
- You two wait for me here.
- Uh, Big Bro...

15:43.108 --> 15:46.195
Caiman. Wait do you remember?

15:46.278 --> 15:47.988
[intriguing music playing]

15:51.659 --> 15:55.621
The feel of this floor...
I think I remember it now...

15:55.704 --> 15:57.915
[pained yelling]

15:57.998 --> 15:59.959
My head is killing me!

16:01.001 --> 16:03.462
What the hell is happening to me?

16:03.545 --> 16:04.463
- [groans]
- [music fades]

16:08.050 --> 16:08.968
[gasps]

16:09.051 --> 16:10.970
[uneasy music playing]

16:11.053 --> 16:12.471
Wait!

16:13.389 --> 16:14.390
[grunts]

16:15.432 --> 16:17.559
What the hell was that?

16:17.643 --> 16:18.852
- [squeaking]
- [gasps]

16:22.189 --> 16:26.110
- Was I... a student here or something?
- [metal rattling underfoot]

16:26.694 --> 16:29.113
Or was I a teacher? A cleaner?

16:30.698 --> 16:32.408
No, that can't be...

16:33.117 --> 16:34.910
That would mean I was a...

16:36.328 --> 16:37.663
or I am...

16:40.124 --> 16:42.543
some kind of sorcerer.

16:43.961 --> 16:46.380
NAKATA
KASHIWABARA

16:46.463 --> 16:49.675
This is... the teacher's room.

16:52.219 --> 16:53.137
Huh?

16:57.224 --> 16:58.517
[gasps]

17:00.310 --> 17:01.270
RISU

17:04.982 --> 17:06.525
[electronic feedback]

17:07.234 --> 17:08.318
[music stops]

17:22.041 --> 17:24.960
[electronic glitching] I'm Aikawa...
[normal voice] Nice to meet you.

17:25.044 --> 17:26.670
[Risu] Nice to meet you too.

17:26.754 --> 17:28.547
I'm... [electronic glitching]

17:28.630 --> 17:30.174
[dramatic music playing]

17:31.759 --> 17:32.634
[door opening]

17:33.385 --> 17:35.554
[music fades]

17:37.723 --> 17:39.058
[dramatic music resumes]

17:41.143 --> 17:42.811
[flies buzzing]

17:44.104 --> 17:45.397
[intense buzzing]

17:46.732 --> 17:48.650
[dramatic music intensifies]

17:57.367 --> 18:03.999
- [screaming]
- [high-pitched electronic feedback]

18:04.666 --> 18:06.502
[unsettling music playing]

18:16.386 --> 18:19.515
Caiman! So there you are! What on earth...

18:19.598 --> 18:20.933
- [gasps]
- [gasps]

18:21.016 --> 18:23.435
- [Natsuki] Big Bro!
- [Nikaido] Caiman!

18:23.519 --> 18:25.938
INFIRMARY

18:26.647 --> 18:29.900
Caiman, what happened in there?

18:30.442 --> 18:33.237
Some of your facial scales
have been ripped off.

18:33.320 --> 18:35.823
- [Natsuki humming]
- Who did this to you? [gasps]

18:37.407 --> 18:40.828
- Don't tell me that you did it yourself?
- [Natsuki gasps]

18:40.911 --> 18:43.330
- Yes, I found it!
- Huh? What's that?

18:43.413 --> 18:45.165
[Natsuki] Bandage masks.

18:45.749 --> 18:47.584
You set it on the head like this.

18:47.668 --> 18:51.547
then press the medicine button,
and pull out the black pin.

18:51.630 --> 18:53.549
Finally, pull the red pins.

18:53.632 --> 18:54.716
Like this?

18:57.427 --> 18:59.805
[smoke hissing, whooshing]

19:00.556 --> 19:02.057
There, all done!

19:02.141 --> 19:04.560
You can even talk and eat
with all this on.

19:04.643 --> 19:06.228
[Nikaido] It's amazing.

19:06.311 --> 19:07.855
[Natsuki] Poor Big Bro...

19:07.938 --> 19:10.858
Something must have made him
hate his face all of a sudden...

19:10.941 --> 19:12.776
- [gasps] Natsuki.
- Huh?

19:12.860 --> 19:15.737
[Nikaido] Can you go buy
something to drink for Caiman?

19:16.238 --> 19:20.117
Uh, sure...
But don't leave me behind, all right?

19:20.200 --> 19:21.869
[footsteps fading]

19:27.457 --> 19:29.251
Caiman, you...

19:29.751 --> 19:31.461
The crosses on your eyes are gone.

19:31.545 --> 19:32.713
[Caiman gasps]

19:32.796 --> 19:35.841
You remembered, right? Something...

19:37.467 --> 19:40.345
Caiman, could it be that

19:41.305 --> 19:43.348
you're a sorcerer too?

19:43.432 --> 19:46.018
[Caiman breathing shakily]

19:46.101 --> 19:49.188
I... I used to go to this school.

19:49.813 --> 19:52.608
And I was here with Risu...

19:52.691 --> 19:54.610
But... but...

19:54.693 --> 19:55.611
[pained groan]

19:55.694 --> 19:56.820
Caiman!

19:57.529 --> 19:59.740
[gasping] Who the hell am I?

20:00.449 --> 20:04.286
I feel something terrifying
raging inside of me.

20:04.870 --> 20:09.291
Nikaido, I might have even hurt you
sometime in the past...

20:09.875 --> 20:12.544
If... if that ever happened, I swear...

20:12.628 --> 20:13.712
[pained yelling]

20:13.795 --> 20:14.796
[Nikaido] Caiman.

20:16.131 --> 20:17.424
You'll be okay.

20:23.138 --> 20:26.058
COME BACK HOME

20:26.141 --> 20:29.394
- [electronic music playing]
- Yoohoo, we're back! Awesome! [laughs]

20:29.478 --> 20:30.520
We're home.

20:31.647 --> 20:33.649
[Shin] You're in the way, Little Bug!

20:34.149 --> 20:36.276
Thank you again, Shin and Noi.

20:36.360 --> 20:38.070
Instead of thanking us,

20:38.153 --> 20:41.531
hurry up and tell us
about the wax figure guy you saw.

20:41.615 --> 20:43.909
You got it. I'll go and change.

20:43.992 --> 20:45.786
Please wait for me in the kotatsu.

20:45.869 --> 20:47.663
[Noi] Kotatsu?

20:50.415 --> 20:53.543
Hey, Shin,
this furniture's really interesting.

20:54.253 --> 20:56.296
- Hey, you're touching my leg!
- [giggles]

20:56.380 --> 20:58.382
- Sorry for the wait.
- C'mon knock it off!

20:58.465 --> 20:59.675
TEST SUBJECT: AI COLEMAN

20:59.758 --> 21:02.928
Professor, isn't that
your most important--

21:03.011 --> 21:06.682
It is. The starting point
of my research on sorcerers.

21:06.765 --> 21:09.184
This is the file where I compiled it all.

21:09.268 --> 21:12.396
So you're saying
this is the wax figure guy?

21:12.479 --> 21:14.690
Ah, his face is totally unrecognizable.

21:14.773 --> 21:18.735
Back then, he was actually
helping me out with my research.

21:19.236 --> 21:22.698
Or rather,
I began the research at his request.

21:23.657 --> 21:26.201
[Shin] Was the guy in this file a human?

21:26.285 --> 21:28.453
Yeah. Without a doubt.

21:28.537 --> 21:31.873
[Shin] The wax figure guy
and the man in this file...

21:32.416 --> 21:34.251
If they're the same person,

21:34.334 --> 21:37.462
then the boss of the Cross-Eyes
would be a human from the Hole.

21:37.546 --> 21:38.797
Huh?

21:38.880 --> 21:42.342
It's true those Cross-Eyes guys
can't use magic...

21:42.843 --> 21:44.511
So it's possible, right?

21:44.594 --> 21:46.638
Kasukabe, where can we find this guy?

21:47.306 --> 21:50.434
[Kasukabe] I think
he was living with his grandfather,

21:50.517 --> 21:52.185
just the two of them.

21:52.269 --> 21:53.895
[intriguing music playing]

21:53.979 --> 21:55.105
COLEMAN

21:55.188 --> 21:56.606
[doorbell buzzing]

21:57.232 --> 21:58.400
Anyone home?

21:58.483 --> 22:00.193
- Noi.
- Roger that!

22:01.320 --> 22:02.946
- [door clattering]
- Huh!

22:05.198 --> 22:07.617
[Kasukabe gasps] Mr. Coleman?!

22:07.701 --> 22:10.746
Hmm. Looks like someone else
managed to beat us here.

22:10.829 --> 22:13.832
Whatever.
Let's find a photo of the grandson.

22:13.915 --> 22:15.959
[sighs] Damn it! Who the hell did this?

22:16.543 --> 22:20.130
Shin, hey! Should we bring this head back
to life with Kikurage's magic?

22:20.213 --> 22:21.840
- Just like we did with Risu?
- [screaming]

22:21.923 --> 22:23.300
- [gasps, screams]
- [Coleman] Ow!

22:23.383 --> 22:26.803
- The... the severed head...
- It just talked?!

22:26.887 --> 22:29.306
[Coleman] Who you calling
severed head, moron?!

22:29.389 --> 22:32.351
I'll have you know
you're looking at a poor victim of magic!

22:32.434 --> 22:34.061
Look! Look at this neck!

22:34.144 --> 22:36.730
They could've at least
made my legs longer too! Gah!

22:36.813 --> 22:38.065
Moronic sorcerers!

22:38.148 --> 22:40.150
Sir, we all thought you were dead.

22:40.233 --> 22:42.903
I was just taking a nap. Who are you guys?

22:42.986 --> 22:45.947
- Well, we're some of your grandson's--
- What're you saying?!

22:46.031 --> 22:48.575
Come on, speak up! I'm hard of hearing.

22:48.658 --> 22:50.577
Oh! I get it!

22:50.660 --> 22:53.580
You guys have come here
to visit my grandson's grave right?

22:53.663 --> 22:55.957
- [both gasp]
- Huh? Visit his grave?!

22:56.792 --> 22:59.044
[Coleman] Ever since
they did this to me last year,

22:59.127 --> 23:01.421
I haven't been able to visit his grave.

23:01.505 --> 23:04.091
You all coming here really helped me out.

23:04.174 --> 23:06.218
It's already been 13 years, huh?

23:06.301 --> 23:09.971
You know, my grandson was killed
by some damn sorcerers.

23:10.889 --> 23:13.725
Now, go on and talk to my grandson.

23:13.809 --> 23:16.978
- All right, let's dig him up.
- You got it!

23:17.062 --> 23:19.064
What?! What did you say?!

23:19.648 --> 23:22.234
- Stop it! What are you doing?
- [shovel digging]

23:22.317 --> 23:25.153
You cursed wretches!! Stop it now!

23:25.237 --> 23:26.488
Knock it off!

23:26.571 --> 23:28.865
Hey! Hey, you! Can't you hear me?!

23:29.449 --> 23:32.411
[Kasukabe] Thirteen years ago,
I attended his funeral.

23:32.494 --> 23:33.370
[Coleman yelling]

23:33.453 --> 23:36.206
[Kasukabe] I saw
his remains buried myself.

23:36.289 --> 23:37.958
If he really is in this grave...

23:38.041 --> 23:38.959
[solid thud]

23:39.042 --> 23:40.460
- [gasps]
- [Coleman] Stop ignoring me!

23:40.544 --> 23:43.213
All right. Here it is. One coffin.

23:43.296 --> 23:45.674
All right then. I'm opening it up!

23:46.216 --> 23:48.218
[Coleman screams] Don't kick it!

23:48.301 --> 23:49.261
[all gasp]

23:49.344 --> 23:50.720
- But this is...
- [screaming]

23:50.804 --> 23:53.723
[Noi] It's empty. Not a damn thing inside.

23:53.807 --> 23:54.933
[dramatic music sting]

23:56.017 --> 23:58.145
[Japanese theme song playing]

25:23.688 --> 25:24.898
THE END

25:24.981 --> 25:27.067
[narrator] What we learned in Episode 15.

25:27.150 --> 25:29.319
Risu and Aikawa are old friends!

25:29.402 --> 25:30.946
Caiman's memories returned...

25:31.029 --> 25:33.448
The Cross-Eyes boss is
an acquaintance of Kasukabe!

25:33.532 --> 25:37.327
What we're going to learn in Episode 16,
it's still... lost in chaos.

25:37.410 --> 25:39.913
- This is... Dorohedoro!
- [music fades out]
